WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:01.922
♪ Mac and cheese, mac and cheese, ♪

00:00:01.922 --> 00:00:04.130
♪ baby, yes, mac and cheese ♪

00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:06.353
Oh, my god, you should do
your mac and cheese dance.

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:13.430
Today I'm gonna be guessing
mac and cheese toppings.

00:00:13.430 --> 00:00:16.430
My friend Shannon has to
guess what these flavors are.

00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:18.610
And I will be blindfolded.

00:00:18.610 --> 00:00:19.443
We don't want to mess up.

00:00:19.443 --> 00:00:21.460
- Can you see anything?
- No.

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:23.428
You better be very descriptive.

00:00:23.428 --> 00:00:26.180
(dramatic fanfare)

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:27.770
This is new technology.

00:00:27.770 --> 00:00:28.950
This is harder than I thought.

00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:31.900
It literally is half a
fork and half a spoon.

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:33.090
I forgot that this part's

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:34.606
gonna make me look like an idiot.

00:00:34.606 --> 00:00:35.439
Ooooh.

00:00:35.439 --> 00:00:36.470
It's crunchy.

00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:37.800
Smoky.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:40.040
Is it more salty?

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:41.730
Let me double-check.

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:43.010
Is it steak?
(buzzer)

00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:45.151
It is cheddar-and-ham mac and cheese.

00:00:45.151 --> 00:00:46.100
(buzzer)

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:47.308
Bacon.

00:00:47.308 --> 00:00:48.141
(bell rings)

00:00:48.141 --> 00:00:49.715
It's so good.

00:00:49.715 --> 00:00:51.236
(laughing)

00:00:51.236 --> 00:00:52.677
Mmmm!

00:00:52.677 --> 00:00:53.560
Oh my god.

00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:54.948
We're here for the mac and cheese.

00:00:54.948 --> 00:00:55.781
We're here.

00:00:55.781 --> 00:00:59.196
(suspenseful music)

00:00:59.196 --> 00:01:00.029
Here we go.

00:01:00.029 --> 00:01:02.070
Oh, ho, okay, this is, this
is gonna be a challenge.

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:04.620
First word that comes to mind.

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:07.560
Backyard...fun?

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:10.680
You put it on food on the 4th of July.

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:11.639
- Bananas.
(buzzer)

00:01:11.639 --> 00:01:12.472
What, wait?

00:01:12.472 --> 00:01:14.040
What are you eating on the 4th of July?

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:15.000
I ate bananas.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.138
So there's onion.

00:01:16.138 --> 00:01:16.971
(bell rings)

00:01:16.971 --> 00:01:17.804
Oh, yeah, I believe there's a meat.

00:01:17.804 --> 00:01:19.310
Okay, so there's a protein.

00:01:19.310 --> 00:01:20.570
It's a brown sauce.

00:01:20.570 --> 00:01:22.070
Maybe it's a little reddish.

00:01:22.070 --> 00:01:23.000
BBQ sauce!

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:23.833
(bell rings)

00:01:23.833 --> 00:01:24.710
- Yes!
- Yeah!

00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:26.190
Our protein is gonna be...

00:01:26.190 --> 00:01:27.090
Cluck, cluck, cluck.

00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:27.923
Chicken.
(bells rings)

00:01:27.923 --> 00:01:28.756
Yes.

00:01:28.756 --> 00:01:29.930
You have to try this.

00:01:29.930 --> 00:01:31.010
You're gonna pass away.

00:01:31.010 --> 00:01:32.820
Oh my god, is it on my face?

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:33.890
Big fan of this.

00:01:33.890 --> 00:01:35.866
Those fried onions, baby.

00:01:35.866 --> 00:01:37.270
Okay, let me have some more.

00:01:37.270 --> 00:01:38.839
I literally had it for a second.

00:01:38.839 --> 00:01:41.890
(suspenseful music)

00:01:41.890 --> 00:01:43.130
Last one was a little rough.

00:01:43.130 --> 00:01:43.963
Yeah.

00:01:43.963 --> 00:01:44.796
- Um...
- Mac and cheese.

00:01:44.796 --> 00:01:46.860
- Yes, that's one.
- Um.

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:49.340
You know that thing that
grows in the ground?

00:01:49.340 --> 00:01:50.173
Vegetables.

00:01:50.173 --> 00:01:53.027
Uh huh, and the thing
that's like purple or white.

00:01:53.027 --> 00:01:54.270
Onion.
(bell rings)

00:01:54.270 --> 00:01:55.103
This is a garnish.

00:01:55.103 --> 00:01:57.340
This is something that makes you fancier.

00:01:57.340 --> 00:01:58.173
Rosemary.
(buzzer)

00:01:58.173 --> 00:01:59.210
Oh, bell pepper.
(buzzer)

00:01:59.210 --> 00:02:00.043
No.

00:02:00.043 --> 00:02:00.876
Bay leaves.
(buzzer)

00:02:00.876 --> 00:02:02.420
- [Man] Oh, my goodness.
- This boy's palate.

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:03.253
Shannon, will you still
be friends with me after?

00:02:03.253 --> 00:02:06.220
All he eats, probably,
is like frozen pizza.

00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:07.190
No.

00:02:07.190 --> 00:02:08.240
Your favorite thing on pizza.

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:09.073
Your favorite thing on pizza.

00:02:09.073 --> 00:02:09.906
Pepperoni.

00:02:09.906 --> 00:02:10.739
No, no.
(buzzer)

00:02:10.739 --> 00:02:11.770
OK, this is something I like.

00:02:11.770 --> 00:02:13.480
Omega-3s baby!

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:14.500
Salmon.
(buzzer)

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:15.333
Close.

00:02:15.333 --> 00:02:16.490
Is it my favorite?

00:02:16.490 --> 00:02:17.670
It is your favorite.

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:18.525
Avocado.
(bell rings)

00:02:18.525 --> 00:02:19.358
Yeah!

00:02:19.358 --> 00:02:21.843
- Pico De Gallo
- Yes.

00:02:22.866 --> 00:02:25.234
Woo!

00:02:25.234 --> 00:02:26.185
Oh my god.

00:02:26.185 --> 00:02:27.930
Mac and cheese is a
foundation for all kinds

00:02:27.930 --> 00:02:29.640
of wonderful creations.

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:31.030
Good job, Panera.

00:02:31.030 --> 00:02:32.133
[Man] I'll get that for you.

00:02:32.133 --> 00:02:32.966
No, no, no, no, no.

00:02:32.966 --> 00:02:33.887
Bring them all back. I
want to try each one again.

00:02:33.887 --> 00:02:35.100
Mm, mm, mm, mm.

00:02:36.966 --> 00:02:38.490
- Oh, good, no, no, no, no.
- Can I have some?

00:02:38.490 --> 00:02:39.323
No.

00:02:39.323 --> 00:02:40.156
Can I have some?

00:02:40.156 --> 00:02:42.906
No, no, no, no, no, no, no, no.

